  "question": {
    "text": "The perpendicular distance, of the line $\\frac{x-1}{2}=\\frac{y+2}{-1}=\\frac{z+3}{2}$ from the point $\\mathrm{P}(2,-10,1)$, is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "9e93L",
      "text": "6",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "iDXH1",
      "text": "$5 \\sqrt{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "jkiCb",
      "text": "$4 \\sqrt{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "mJPb2",
      "text": "$3 \\sqrt{5}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/CYRrWAIzJQ0eqdr_Q5Cks64tJO7nBi8021kTOezNHYw.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n\n\n\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\left.\\frac{\\mathrm{x}-1}{2}=\\frac{\\mathrm{y}+2}{-1}=\\frac{\\mathrm{z}+3}{2}=\\lambda \\text { (let }\\right) \\\\ & (2 \\lambda+1,-\\lambda-2,2 \\lambda-3) \\\\ & \\because \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{PA}} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{n}}=0 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow(2 \\lambda-1) 2+(-\\lambda+8)(-1)+(2 \\lambda-4) 2=0 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow 4 \\lambda-2+\\lambda-8+4 \\lambda-8=0 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow 9 \\lambda-18=0 \\Rightarrow \\lambda=2 \\\\ & \\therefore \\mathrm{~A}(5,-4,1) \\\\ & \\therefore \\mathrm{AP}=\\sqrt{3^2+6^2+0^2}=\\sqrt{45}=3 \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
